<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Solar installation in Lagos usually starts with the same problem: light that comes and goes, and a gen that eats petrol to cover the gaps. As an illustration, a 3.0 kVA generator running about 5 hours a day at about 1.25 litres an hour (Nigerian retailer Jamara Home says the Sumec Firman ECO4990ES runs up to 12 hours at 50% load on a 15 L tank, and 15 / 12 = 1.25) and petrol at N1,400 a litre (a Lagos pump price reported by Vanguard on 10-11 October 2026) costs 1.25 x 5 x 1,400 = N8,750 a day. That is an example, not a prediction for your house.</p><p>This site is advertising for independent Nigerian solar installers. It does not install or sell anything itself. Call now with your area and what you want to run, and ask for an independent installer to send a written quote you can compare with two others.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Lagos</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Lagos Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Home solar installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hybrid inverter, battery and panels for duplexes and flats in Ikeja, Surulere, Yaba, Lekki and Ajah estates. The installer should work from a load audit of your own appliances.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Inverter and battery installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For Lagos homes whose old inverter and tubular batteries no longer last the night. Ask for lithium and tubular options quoted side by side, with the exact battery model on paper.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Commercial solar</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For shops, schools, clinics, churches and small offices from Ikorodu to Festac that want to cut diesel. Ask for the load assessment and the changeover arrangement in writing.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Solar and inverter repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For a system that keeps tripping or a battery bank that has gone weak. An installer should check wiring, protection and settings before blaming the equipment.</p>
      </div>
</div>
